{"summary":"Implements FB_GateTelemetry with reset priority, strict timing-parameter validation, sequence-inequality freshness, saturating age accumulation, latched comm fault cleared only by fresh+Ack, and derived remote-write permit. Sequence history and age are preserved on illegal parameters.","code":"FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_GateTelemetry
VAR_INPUT
  Reset : BOOL;
  FrameValid : BOOL;
  FrameSeq : UDINT;
  Ack : BOOL;
  DtMs : UDINT;
  TimeoutMs : UDINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
  Fresh : BOOL;
  AgeMs : UDINT;
  CommFault : BOOL;
  RemoteWritePermit : BOOL;
  Error : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
  known : BOOL;
  seq : UDINT;
  age : UDINT;
  fault : BOOL;
  validTiming : BOOL;
  freshNow : BOOL;
END_VAR

validTiming := (DtMs >= 1) AND (DtMs <= 1000) AND (TimeoutMs >= 1) AND (TimeoutMs <= 60000);

IF Reset THEN
  known := FALSE;
  seq := 0;
  age := 0;
  fault := TRUE;
  Fresh := FALSE;
  AgeMs := 0;
  CommFault := TRUE;
  RemoteWritePermit := FALSE;
  Error := FALSE;
ELSIF NOT validTiming THEN
  fault := TRUE;
  Fresh := FALSE;
  AgeMs := age;
  CommFault := TRUE;
  RemoteWritePermit := FALSE;
  Error := TRUE;
ELSE
  Error := FALSE;

  freshNow := FrameValid AND ((NOT known) OR (FrameSeq <> seq));

  IF freshNow THEN
    known := TRUE;
    seq := FrameSeq;
    age := 0;
  ELSE
    IF age + DtMs > 60000 THEN
      age := 60000;
    ELSE
      age := age + DtMs;
    END_IF;
  END_IF;

  Fresh := freshNow;
  AgeMs := age;

  IF freshNow AND Ack THEN
    fault := FALSE;
  ELSIF age >= TimeoutMs THEN
    fault := TRUE;
  END_IF;

  CommFault := fault;
  RemoteWritePermit := (NOT fault) AND (age < TimeoutMs);
END_IF;

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK"}

reasoning_content:
We need to implement FB_GateTelemetry in ST.

State: known (BOOL), seq (UDINT), age (AgeMs output), fault (CommFault output). Outputs: Fresh, AgeMs, CommFault, RemoteWritePermit, Error.

Logic:

Reset: known=FALSE, seq=0, age=0, fault=TRUE, Fresh=FALSE, Error=FALSE, RemoteWritePermit=FALSE.

Else if invalid timing (DtMs<1 or >1000 or TimeoutMs<1 or >60000): Error=TRUE, CommFault=TRUE, RemoteWritePermit=FALSE, Fresh=FALSE; keep known/seq/age.

Else: Error=FALSE; Fresh := FrameValid AND (NOT known OR FrameSeq <> seq). If Fresh: known=TRUE, seq=FrameSeq, age=0. Else age := MIN(60000, age+DtMs).

fault: start from previous fault; if age >= TimeoutMs then set fault TRUE; if Fresh AND Ack then clear fault FALSE.

Order matters: fault latch condition uses new age. Spec: "fault从pre.fault开始，age>=TimeoutMs时置位，fresh AND Ack时清除". If both set, what's the order? In LTL P06: (!Reset & validTiming & fresh & Ack) -> (!CommFault & RemoteWritePermit). That implies clear wins over set when fresh&Ack. Actually if age>=Timeout (age is 0 when fresh, so age>=TimeoutMs can't happen when fresh since TimeoutMs>=1 and age=0). So no conflict. But with clamp, fine.

Careful: when Fresh, age=0 so age>=TimeoutMs false. So clear condition just Fresh&Ack -> fault FALSE.

Implement with IF/ELSIF.

Note: RemoteWritePermit := NOT Reset AND NOT Error AND NOT fault AND age < TimeoutMs. In invalid timing branch, timeout might be invalid; permit = FALSE. In reset, FALSE.

Also in reset branch Error=FALSE explicitly.

Let me write:

```
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_GateTelemetry
VAR_INPUT
  Reset : BOOL;
  FrameValid : BOOL;
  FrameSeq : UDINT;
  Ack : BOOL;
  DtMs : UDINT;
  TimeoutMs : UDINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
  Fresh : BOOL;
  AgeMs : UDINT;
  CommFault : BOOL;
  RemoteWritePermit : BOOL;
  Error : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
  known : BOOL;
  seq : UDINT;
  age : UDINT;
  fault : BOOL;
  validTiming : BOOL;
  freshNow : BOOL;
END_VAR

validTiming := (DtMs >= 1) AND (DtMs <= 1000) AND (TimeoutMs >= 1) AND (TimeoutMs <= 60000);

IF Reset THEN
  known := FALSE;
  seq := 0;
  age := 0;
  fault := TRUE;
  Fresh := FALSE;
  AgeMs := 0;
  CommFault := TRUE;
  RemoteWritePermit := FALSE;
  Error := FALSE;
ELSIF NOT validTiming THEN
  Fresh := FALSE;
  Error := TRUE;
  fault := TRUE;
  CommFault := TRUE;
  RemoteWritePermit := FALSE;
  AgeMs := age;
ELSE
  Error := FALSE;
  freshNow := FrameValid AND ((NOT known) OR (FrameSeq <> seq));
  IF freshNow THEN
    known := TRUE;
    seq := FrameSeq;
    age := 0;
  ELSE
    IF age + DtMs > 60000 THEN
      age := 60000;
    ELSE
      age := age + DtMs;
    END_IF;
  END_IF;
  Fresh := freshNow;
  AgeMs := age;
  IF freshNow AND Ack THEN
    fault := FALSE;
  ELSIF age >= TimeoutMs THEN
    fault := TRUE;
  END_IF;
  CommFault := fault;
  RemoteWritePermit := (NOT fault) AND (age < TimeoutMs);
END_IF;
END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
```

Wait: in the Else valid case, if fault was previously false and age >= timeout, latch fault TRUE. If fault previously true and fresh&Ack, clear. If fault true but not fresh&Ack, stays true. Good. But order: if fresh&Ack AND age>=TimeoutMs — can't happen since fresh sets age=0 and TimeoutMs>=1. So ELSIF fine. Actually to be safe, use IF fresh AND Ack THEN fault:=FALSE; END_IF; IF age>=TimeoutMs THEN fault:=TRUE; END_IF; — but that would set fault TRUE when fresh&Ack if age>=Timeout... age=0, impossible. Keep ELSIF or separate. Use separate but with fresh age=0 guarantee. Actually safer to do clear-wins per P06. Use:

IF freshNow AND Ack THEN fault := FALSE; END_IF;
IF age >= TimeoutMs AND NOT (freshNow AND Ack) THEN fault := TRUE; END_IF;

But simpler: IF freshNow AND Ack THEN fault := FALSE; ELSIF age >= TimeoutMs THEN fault := TRUE; END_IF; — that's fine.

One nuance: overflow on age + DtMs. Age max 60000, DtMs max 1000, so max 61000, no overflow in UDINT. Fine.

P05 requires when not fresh, AgeMs = min(60000, pre.age+DtMs). Done.

P03 reset: AgeMs=0, CommFault, !Fresh, !Permit, !Error. Done.

P04 invalid timing: Error & CommFault & !Fresh & !Permit & ageHeld. Done (age unchanged, AgeMs := age).

Note: In invalid branch, fault := TRUE sets internal fault; CommFault := TRUE. Good.

Also in the legal branch when Error cleared — yes.

One subtlety: after Reset, on next call, known=FALSE, so first frame is fresh. Good.

RemoteWritePermit in legal branch computed. Should also ensure that after Reset, RemoteWritePermit false. Done.

Note requirement: "Clear it only on a call with both Fresh=TRUE and Ack=TRUE." Fresh being the computed fresh. Done.

Also RemoteWritePermit equality: permit := !Reset AND !err AND !fault AND age<TimeoutMs. In legal branch Error=FALSE, Reset=FALSE. Good.

Type declarations: no new TYPE needed.

